Q('C1-L082','Exam Lab 2 (TOEFL · IELTS · college)',
 'eu consigo treinar a descrição de um gráfico em texto (infográfico), como na tarefa de escrita do IELTS.',
 ('Reading · An infographic in text',info('Greetings Around the World: A Survey of 1,000 Professionals',[('Handshake','52% — most common in business'),('Bow','18% — common in parts of East Asia'),('Cheek kiss','15% — common in parts of Europe and Latin America'),('Nod or smile only','10% — more frequent online'),('Other','5%')],note='Source: fictional survey for practice. Notice the verbs: **account for**, **make up**, **rank second**.',gloss=[('survey','pesquisa'),('account for','representar'),('rank','ficar na posição')])),
 [('The handshake is the most common greeting in the survey.','T','52%.'),('Bowing accounts for more than half of the answers.','F','18%.'),('The survey was done in 2020.','NG','data não informada.')],
 [('“account for” (percentages) = ?',['representar','prestar contas','explicar'],0,'account for = representar.'),('“rank” = ?',['ficar na posição','tipo de classe','rancor'],0,'rank = classificar.')],
 G('Descrever dados: linguagem para gráficos',['Função','Estrutura','Exemplo'],[['maior','The highest figure is…','**The highest figure** is the handshake.'],['parte','X accounts for Y%','Bowing **accounts for** 18%.'],['comparar','almost twice as…','Handshakes are **almost three times** as common as bows.'],['resumo','Overall,…','**Overall**, handshakes dominate.']],'Comece com uma frase geral (**overall**), depois cite os números mais **importantes**; não descreva cada número.','Use **the** + superlativo: *the most common*, *the lowest*.'),
 [('The handshake ___ for 52% of answers. (account)','accounts','accounts for.',None),('___, handshakes dominate. (Overall)','Overall','resumo.',None),('Bowing is the ___ common greeting after the handshake. (second)','second','second most.',None),('A cheek kiss is ___ as common as a nod. (half)','half','proporção.',None)],
 V('survey result=resultado da pesquisa|greeting habit=hábito de saudação|bar chart=gráfico de barras|pie chart=gráfico de pizza|line graph=gráfico de linhas|percentage point=ponto percentual|overall trend=tendência geral|highest figure=maior valor|lowest figure=menor valor|sharp rise=aumento acentuado|steady decline=queda constante|slight increase=ligeiro aumento|data source=fonte de dados|key feature=característica principal|visual summary=resumo visual|comparison phrase=expressão de comparação|handshake custom=costume do aperto de mão|cheek kiss=beijo no rosto|formal bow=reverência formal|nod gesture=aceno de cabeça|online greeting=saudação online|survey sample=amostra da pesquisa|age group=faixa etária|regional difference=diferença regional|task response=resposta à tarefa|word count=contagem de palavras|chart title=título do gráfico|axis label=rótulo do eixo'),
 ('Writing class',[('Teacher','How should we begin the description?','Como devemos começar a descrição?'),('Student','With an overall statement about the main trend.','Com uma afirmação geral sobre a tendência principal.'),('Teacher','And then?','E depois?'),('Student','Highlight the key figures and make comparisons.','Destacar os números principais e fazer comparações.')]),
 [('Describe the main figure in the infographic.','Descreva.','The handshake accounts for just over half of the answers.'),('Compare two figures.','Compare.','Handshakes are almost three times as common as bows.'),('Give an overall summary.','Resuma.','Overall, traditional greetings remain popular.')],
 ('Write a 6-sentence summary of the infographic, with an overview and two comparisons.','The chart shows how 1,000 professionals greet each other. Overall, the handshake is by far the most common greeting. It accounts for 52% of answers. Bowing ranks second with 18%, followed by the cheek kiss at 15%. Nodding or smiling only makes up 10%. Other greetings are rare.',['Escrevi uma **visão geral**','Usei **account for / make up**','Fiz **comparações**'],'6 frases'),
 exam=['IELTS Writing Task 1: escreva 150 palavras; visão geral + detalhes principais, sem opinião.','Use verbos de dados (account for, rise, fall, rank) e comparações (almost twice as…).','Reserve 3 minutos para checar números e unidades.'],
 verbs=[('depict','retratar; descrever','The chart depicts greeting habits.','It depicts a clear trend.')],
 expr=[('By far the most…','De longe o mais…'),('Just over half','Um pouco mais da metade'),('A significant minority','Uma minoria significativa'),('Account for a large share','Representar grande parte'),('Roughly one in five','Cerca de um em cada cinco'),('The vast majority','A grande maioria'),('Stand out from the rest','Destacar-se dos demais'),('Lag behind','Ficar atrás')],pron=PP)
Q('C1-L083','Perfect participle passive — practice and contrast',
 'eu consigo contrastar having been + particípio com being + particípio e com having + particípio, num podcast.',
 ('Reading · A podcast transcript',text('Podcast: Language at Work, Episode 12',['Welcome back. Today: three similar structures. **Having finished** the report, Ana sent it. That is active: she did the action. **Having been finished** late, the report was ignored. That is passive: it received the action.','Now compare **being asked** with **having been asked**. **Being asked** to speak, he felt nervous (at the same time). **Having been asked** to speak twice, he finally agreed (earlier, then later).','So remember: **having + participle** for earlier active actions, **having been + participle** for earlier passive actions, and **being + participle** for the same time.'],kicker='PODCAST',by='Host: Ellis Moreau (fictional)',gloss=[('ignore','ignorar'),('nervous','nervoso'),('earlier','antes'),('compare','comparar')])),
 [('“Having finished the report, Ana sent it” is active.','T','she did the action.'),('“Being asked” shows an earlier action.','F','same time.'),('The host says the structures are completely different.','F','three similar structures.')],
 [('“earlier” = ?',['anterior','mais cedo ainda','cedo demais'],0,'earlier = antes.'),('“nervous” = ?',['nervoso','cortês','novo'],0,'nervous = nervoso.')],
 G('Contraste de formas',['Forma','Tempo','Exemplo'],[['Having + particípio','ação ativa anterior','**Having read** it, she agreed.'],['Having been + particípio','ação passiva anterior','**Having been read** aloud, it moved us.'],['Being + particípio','ação passiva simultânea','**Being asked**, he felt nervous.'],['Not having been + particípio','passiva negativa anterior','**Not having been told**, I stayed.']],'Pergunte: a ação veio **antes** ou é **simultânea**? Quem faz a ação: o sujeito (**ativa**) ou outra pessoa (**passiva**)?','**Being** + particípio descreve ação simultânea; ✗ *Being told earlier* para ação anterior.'),
 [('___ finished the report, Ana sent it. (Having)','Having','ativa anterior.',None),('___ been warned twice, he finally agreed. (Having)','Having','passiva anterior.',None),('___ asked to speak, he felt nervous. (Being)','Being','simultânea.',None),('Not having been ___ , I stayed home. (tell)','told','particípio.',None)],
 V('podcast host=apresentador de podcast|episode title=título do episódio|sound bite=trecho de áudio|grammar point=ponto gramatical|participle clause=oração participial|active voice=voz ativa|passive voice=voz passiva|earlier action=ação anterior|same-time action=ação simultânea|sentence pattern=padrão de frase|contrast chart=quadro de contraste|listening note=anotação de escuta|show notes=notas do programa|guest speaker=palestrante convidado|audience question=pergunta do público|time marker=marcador de tempo|clause subject=sujeito da oração|formal writing=escrita formal|spoken narrative=narrativa falada|stylistic choice=escolha estilística|word order=ordem das palavras|tense sequence=sequência de tempos|usage note=nota de uso|common slip=deslize comum|self-correction=autocorreção|clear example=exemplo claro|quick recap=resumo rápido|learner error=erro de aprendiz'),
 ('Studio',[('Host','So which is passive: having read or having been read?','Então qual é passiva: having read ou having been read?'),('Guest','Having been read is passive. The subject receives the action.','Having been read é passiva. O sujeito recebe a ação.'),('Host','And being asked?','E being asked?'),('Guest','It is passive too, but the actions happen at the same time.','Também é passiva, mas as ações acontecem ao mesmo tempo.')]),
 [('Make a sentence with having been + participle.','Faça.','Having been told the truth, she changed her mind.'),('Make a sentence with being + participle.','Faça.','Being asked to speak, he blushed.'),('Explain the difference aloud.','Explique.','Having been asked is earlier; being asked is at the same time.')],
 ('Write 5 sentences contrasting having + participle, having been + participle and being + participle.','Having finished the draft, I sent it. Having been finished late, it was ignored. Being asked to speak, I felt nervous. Having been asked twice, I agreed. Not having been told, I stayed home.',['Usei as **três formas**','Verifiquei o **sujeito**','Marquei **antes** e **ao mesmo tempo**'],'5 frases'),
 verbs=[('contrast','contrastar','We contrast the two forms.','It contrasts with the active one.')],
 expr=[('Strictly speaking,…','A rigor,…'),('To be on the safe side,…','Por segurança,…'),('The rule of thumb is…','A regra geral é…'),('Get the wrong end of the stick.','Entender tudo errado.'),('Split hairs.','Ficar com minúcias.'),('A fine line between…','Uma linha tênue entre…'),('As a general rule,…','Como regra geral,…'),('By the same token,…','Pela mesma razão,…')],pron=PX)
Q('C1-L084','Exam Lab 3 (TOEFL · IELTS · college)',
 'eu consigo treinar um resumo de notícia e usar illustrate e Be that as it may… para introduzir um contraste.',
 ('Reading · A news report',news('Report: Translation Apps Improve, but Misunderstandings Persist',['A new study of 2,000 international students finds that translation apps have **improved** daily communication, but serious **misunderstandings** remain. “The tools **illustrate** how far technology has come,” said linguist Rui Alves. “**Be that as it may**, they still miss tone, humour and politeness.”','One example **illustrates** the problem: an app turned a polite request into an order. Students who checked important messages with a human reader made far fewer mistakes. The university plans a free **peer-review** service next term.'],kicker='EDUCATION',by='By Camila Ortiz',gloss=[('persist','persistir'),('tone','tom'),('politeness','cortesia'),('peer review','revisão por colegas')])),
 [('The study found that translation apps have not improved.','F','have improved.'),('An app turned a polite request into an order.','T','one example.'),('The university already offers the review service.','F','plans … next term.')],
 [('“persist” = ?',['persistir','permitir','perseguir'],0,'persist = persistir.'),('“Be that as it may” introduces …',['um contraste','uma condição','um exemplo'],0,'Be that as it may = apesar disso.')],
 G('Resumir uma notícia (TOEFL)',['Passo','O que fazer','Exemplo'],[['1. Ideia central','uma frase com os fatos principais','A study finds that apps improve communication.'],['2. Detalhes','1–2 dados ou exemplos','An app turned a request into an order.'],['3. Contraste','**Be that as it may…**','**Be that as it may**, tone is still missed.'],['4. Palavras próprias','parafrasear, não copiar','students → learners']],'No resumo, **parafraseie**: troque palavras e estrutura, mantendo o sentido. Use **illustrate** para introduzir um exemplo.','Copiar frases do texto pode anular a pontuação.'),
 [('This example ___ the problem. (illustrate)','illustrates','3ª pessoa.',None),('___ that as it may, tone is still missed. (Be)','Be','Be that as it may.',None),('Summaries should ___ the text, not copy it. (paraphrase)','paraphrase','parafrasear.',None),('A study of 2,000 students ___ that apps help. (find)','finds','presente da notícia.',None)],
 V('translation app=aplicativo de tradução|international student=estudante internacional|daily communication=comunicação diária|serious misunderstanding=mal-entendido grave|polite request=pedido cortês|human reader=leitor humano|peer-review service=serviço de revisão por colegas|campus news=notícias do campus|news summary=resumo de notícia|main idea=ideia central|key detail=detalhe-chave|paraphrase skill=habilidade de parafrasear|source text=texto-fonte|integrated task=tarefa integrada|response time=tempo de resposta|speech recognition=reconhecimento de fala|machine translation=tradução automática|language tool=ferramenta de idioma|tone of voice=tom de voz|humour gap=lacuna de humor|study finding=resultado do estudo|linguist’s warning=alerta do linguista|funding source=fonte de financiamento|policy plan=plano de política|next term=próximo semestre|free service=serviço gratuito|accuracy rate=taxa de precisão|reading speed=velocidade de leitura'),
 ('Test prep',[('Tutor','How do you summarise this article?','Como você resume esta notícia?'),('Student','Apps help students, but they still miss tone.','Aplicativos ajudam estudantes, mas ainda perdem o tom.'),('Tutor','Good. Add a contrast marker.','Bom. Acrescente um marcador de contraste.'),('Student','Be that as it may, human readers make fewer errors.','Apesar disso, leitores humanos cometem menos erros.')]),
 [('Summarise the news in one sentence.','Resuma.','A study finds that translation apps help but still miss tone.'),('Give an example that illustrates the problem.','Dê.','One example illustrates it: a polite request became an order.'),('Use Be that as it may…','Use.','Be that as it may, human checking still matters.')],
 ('Write a 4-sentence summary of the news report, in your own words.','A recent study suggests that translation apps make everyday communication easier for international students. One example illustrates a persistent weakness: politeness is often lost. Be that as it may, students who asked a human to check key messages made fewer mistakes. The university will offer a free review service next term.',['Parafraseei o texto','Usei **illustrate**','Usei **Be that as it may…**'],'4 frases'),
 exam=['TOEFL Writing (integrated): resuma os pontos principais com suas palavras; não dê opinião.','Anote ideia central, 2 detalhes e o contraste do texto antes de escrever.','Releia procurando cópia literal; troque estrutura e vocabulário.'],
 verbs=[('illustrate','ilustrar; exemplificar','We illustrate every claim.','This chart illustrates the trend.')],
 expr=[('Be that as it may…','Seja como for…'),('Having said that,…','Dito isso,…'),('Nonetheless,…','Ainda assim,…'),('All the same,…','Mesmo assim,…'),('On the other hand,…','Por outro lado,…'),('In spite of this,…','Apesar disso,…'),('That said,…','Dito isso,…'),('Even so,…','Mesmo assim,…')],pron=PO)
Q('C1-L085','Perfect participle passive — production and review',
 'eu consigo produzir uma biografia curta com having been + particípio e revisar a forma e o sujeito.',
 ('Reading · A short biography',bio('Amara Okoye (fictional interpreter)',['**Having been raised** in a bilingual household, Amara Okoye could switch between languages before she could read. **Having been rejected** by her first-choice university, she trained at night while working as a guide. **Not having been trusted** with major assignments at first, she volunteered for hospital interpreting.','**Having been recognised** for her calm under pressure, she was chosen to interpret at an international peace forum. **Having been asked** about her secret, she says: “I listen twice as much as I speak.”'],years='Fictional character',facts=[('Job','intérprete'),('Skill','dois idiomas'),('Lesson','ouvir antes de falar')],gloss=[('raise','criar'),('reject','rejeitar'),('trust','confiar'),('forum','fórum')])),
 [('Amara grew up speaking one language.','F','bilingual household.'),('She trained at night.','T','trained at night.'),('She says she speaks twice as much as she listens.','F','listen twice as much.')],
 [('“bilingual” = ?',['bilíngue','duplo','balanceado'],0,'bilingual = bilíngue.'),('“forum” = ?',['fórum','ferro','forma'],0,'forum = fórum.')],
 G('Checklist: Perfect participle passive',['Verifique','Exemplo'],[['Having been + particípio','**Having been raised** abroad, she…'],['Not having been + particípio','**Not having been trusted**, she volunteered.'],['Mesmo sujeito','she… / she… (não *the job*)'],['Ação anterior','a participial vem **antes** da principal'],['Vírgula','vírgula depois da oração participial']],'Na produção, revise três coisas: **forma** (having been), **sujeito** (o mesmo) e **tempo** (anterior).','✗ *Having been rejected, the job was lost.* (sujeito errado).'),
 [('___ been raised abroad, she spoke two languages. (Having)','Having','Having been.',None),('Not having been ___ , she volunteered. (trust)','trusted','particípio.',None),('Having been recognised, ___ was chosen to interpret. (she)','she','mesmo sujeito.',None),('Having been rejected, she trained at ___ . (night)','night','information.',None)],
 V('bilingual household=lar bilíngue|first-choice university=universidade de primeira escolha|night course=curso noturno|hospital interpreting=interpretação hospitalar|peace forum=fórum de paz|simultaneous interpreter=intérprete simultâneo|conference booth=cabine de conferência|language pair=par de idiomas|source language=língua de origem|target language=língua de chegada|interpreting error=erro de interpretação|sight translation=tradução à primeira vista|professional ethics=ética profissional|confidential matter=assunto confidencial|bilingual upbringing=criação bilíngue|career turning point=ponto de virada na carreira|early setback=contratempo inicial|steady progress=progresso constante|public recognition=reconhecimento público|calm delivery=entrega calma|crisis meeting=reunião de crise|peace envoy=enviado de paz|volunteer work=trabalho voluntário|biographical detail=detalhe biográfico|life story=história de vida|career path=trajetória profissional|personal motto=lema pessoal|quiet strength=força silenciosa'),
 ('Interview',[('Host','Having been rejected, how did you continue?','Tendo sido rejeitada, como continuou?'),('Amara','Having been told no once, I trained at night.','Tendo ouvido não uma vez, treinei à noite.'),('Host','What is your secret?','Qual é o seu segredo?'),('Amara','I listen twice as much as I speak.','Escuto duas vezes mais do que falo.')]),
 [('Tell a person’s story with having been.','Conte.','Having been raised abroad, she spoke two languages.'),('Explain a setback.','Explique.','Having been rejected, she tried again.'),('Revise a wrong sentence aloud.','Corrija.','Having been rejected, she trained at night.')],
 ('Write a 6-sentence mini-biography of a real or fictional person using having been + participle at least three times.','Having been born in a small town, Lia dreamed of travelling. Having been refused a scholarship, she worked for two years. Not having been discouraged, she applied again. Having been accepted at last, she moved to Lisbon. Having been trained as an interpreter, she now works at conferences.',['Usei **Having been** três vezes','Verifiquei o **sujeito**','Coloquei **vírgula**'],'6 frases'),
 verbs=[('recognise','reconhecer','We recognise good work.','She recognises every accent.')],
 expr=[('Against all odds,…','Contra todas as probabilidades,…'),('Rise through the ranks.','Subir na carreira.'),('Turn the tables.','Virar o jogo.'),('Find one’s voice.','Encontrar a própria voz.'),('Make a name for oneself.','Fazer nome.'),('Learn the ropes.','Aprender o ofício.'),('A steep learning curve.','Uma curva de aprendizado íngreme.'),('Stand one’s ground.','Manter-se firme.')],pron=PE)
build_index();print('ok')
